g only the ADR/issue pointer; an on-call engineer reading this table during an incident loses the in-code guidance on what action to take.","introduced":true}]}],"findings":[{"file":"core/pipeline/dispatch-rc.sh","category":"observability","line":166,"severity":"low","lenses":["sre"],"messages":["The comment rewrite drops the operator-actionable recovery hint 'more budget, or the work must shrink' from the rc=10 row, leaving only the ADR/issue pointer; an on-call engineer reading this table during an incident loses the in-code guidance on what action to take."]}],"pre_existing":[{"file":"plugins/agent/review-report/plugin.sh","category":"partial-delivery","line":166,"severity":"low","lenses":["scope"],"messages":["The issue explicitly lists plugins/agent/review-report/plugin.sh:166 ('comment cites exhausted') as one of seven sites to retire, but the design reduced the list to six edits and omitted this file from both the planned scope and the diff; the R-4 acceptance grep covers $REPO_ROOT/plugins/ and the tests passed (824/0), suggesting the comment form does not match the grep patterns, but the explicit issue listing indicates prescriptive intent that was not delivered."]}],"summary":"1 merge-readiness finding(s) across 6 lens(es) (0 critical, 0 high).","escalation_note":"One or more lenses scored <=3 or found a critical-severity issue; consider requesting a tier-2 expert review or escalating to a senior reviewer before merging. Advisory only — this does not block the pipeline."}
